IP Address Input – Takes IP address and CIDR prefix from the user.
Network Calculation – Finds the original network address, subnet mask, CIDR, and broadcast address.
Number of Subnets – Takes the required number of subnets.
Bits Borrowed – Calculates how many host bits need to be borrowed.
New Subnet Mask – Calculates the new CIDR and subnet mask.
Subnet Details – Displays for each subnet:
Network address
Subnet mask
CIDR
First host
Last host
Broadcast address
Total addresses
Usable hosts
Validation – Checks invalid IP/CIDR and invalid number of subnets.
Final Output – Displays that subnetting was completed successfully


